      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To solve for \\( y \\) given the equation \\( x^2 + x + 4 = y - 4 \\) and the value \\( x = -7 \\), we will follow these steps:\n\n1. Substitute \\( x = -7 \\) into the equation.\n2. Simplify the left-hand side of the equation.\n3. Isolate \\( y \\) on one side of the equation.\n\nLet's start with the substitution:\n\n\\[ x^2 + x + 4 = y - 4 \\]\n\\[ (-7)^2 + (-7) + 4 = y - 4 \\]\n\nNext, we calculate \\( (-7)^2 \\):\n\n\\[ (-7)^2 = 49 \\]\nSo the equation becomes:\n\\[ 49 - 7 + 4 = y - 4 \\]\n\nNow, we simplify the left-hand side:\n\n\\[ 49 - 7 = 42 \\]\n\\[ 42 + 4 = 46 \\]\nSo the equation is now:\n\\[ 46 = y - 4 \\]\n\nTo solve for \\( y \\), we add 4 to both sides of the equation:\n\n\\[ 46 + 4 = y \\]\n\\[ 50 = y \\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\( y \\) is \\(\\boxed{50}\\).",
